{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>Therefore.</b> The argument: you trusted in the money you gave to the king of Assyria, that he would not come. This iniquity will destroy you." "<b>Like a breach [fallen, swelling].</b> Like a falling tower, or a swelling thing; it is from the root of נפוח, from the derivation of אבעבועות (Exodus 9:9). Or נבעה may be an adjective of פרץ." "<b>Suddenly</b> and <b>suddenly</b> are near in meaning, like the sense of עפר (dust)."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:55:59.187987824Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}